    "summary": "Fire‑filled Keith keys, killer Truckin’, seamless segues",
    "blurb": "The set bursts with a scorching China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider jam and a tight Truckin' performance, while the second set flows through Big River into Playing In The Band and He’s Gone with flawless transitions. Jerry delivers smoky, extra‑chops solos; Keith Godchaux is on fire at the keys. Recommended for its vibrant country‑rock feel and strong recordings.",
    "review": "On October 27, 1973 the Dead took the Indianapolis State Fair Coliseum into a high‑octane country‑rock groove that still shines in the best available tapes. The first set builds momentum with a blistering China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider pair and a Truckin' that showcases Jerry’s “extra chops” and Keith’s relentless, fire‑on‑the‑keys solo on Beat It On Down The Line. The second set is a masterclass in flow: Big River slides into a Playing In The Band reprise, leading into an inspired He’s Gone, then a soaring sequence of Truckin' → Nobody’s Fault But Mine → Wharf Rat → Stella Blue that feels both tight and exploratory. Jerry’s vocal nuance on Sugaree and the band’s overall country‑rock swagger are captured nicely in the audience tape, while the top soundboard (gd73-10-27.sbd.wier.16583.sbeok.shnf) offers crystal‑clear mids after an initial warm‑up, preserving the energy of those jams. For fans seeking both musical fireworks and a reliable listening experience, this show is a must‑hear.",
